<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Vercingetorix</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 82–<a href="/years/46-bce">46 BCE</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Vercingetorix was a chief of the Arverni who in 52 BCE united most of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gauls">Gauls</a> in revolt against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/julius-caesar">Julius Caesar</a>. He used scorched-earth tactics and repulsed Caesar at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gergovia">Gergovia</a>, but was besieged at Alesia, the town of the Mandubii, and surrendered when a relief army failed. He was displayed in Caesar's triumph in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> and executed.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/vercingetorix.jpg" alt="Vercingetorix" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Vercing%C3%A9torix_stat%C3%A8re_Gallica_avers.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
